The class `NumberTools` contains static methods for working with the digits of positive integers.

```java
public class NumberTools {
    /** Returns the sum of the digits of n. Precondition: n > 0 */
    public static int digitSum(int n) { /* part (a) */ }
    /** Returns how many integers from lo to hi, inclusive, have a digit sum divisible by k.
        Precondition: 0 < lo <= hi, k > 0 */
    public static int countDivisible(int lo, int hi, int k) { /* part (b) */ }
}
```

For example, `digitSum(1772)` returns 17, and `countDivisible(24, 42, 6)` returns 4.

A `ScoreKeeper` records the scores of one player. The class also tracks the total number of scores recorded by all ScoreKeeper objects.


• `ScoreKeeper(String name)` creates a keeper with no scores.

• `void addScore(int s)` records a score.

• `double getAverage()` returns the average score, or 0.0 if there are none.

• `int getBest()` returns the highest score, or -1 if there are none.

• `static int getTotalScores()` returns the number of scores recorded by all keepers.

Example:

```java
ScoreKeeper a = new ScoreKeeper("Ben");
ScoreKeeper b = new ScoreKeeper("Hana");
a.addScore(64);
a.addScore(64);
a.addScore(77);
b.addScore(80);
b.addScore(76);
a.getAverage();               // returns 68.333
a.getBest();                  // returns 77
ScoreKeeper.getTotalScores(); // returns 5
```

